WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.400
as you walk down the halls of the scp foundation&nbsp;
site 19 speaking in the various windows at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.640
anomalies contained there you might catch a&nbsp;
glimpse of a dark figure bent over a table&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:18.880
tinkering away like an artisan in his workshop&nbsp;
a vintage black apothecary bag sits next to him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.160
open and if you stop and watch for a while&nbsp;
you'll see him pull all manner of tools out of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:31.920
impossibly large tools things that shouldn't fit&nbsp;
in such a small bag a bone saw an iv stand jars of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.360
fluorescent liquids and needles the length&nbsp;
of your forearm you shouldn't be surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:44.000
this is a place for impossible things after all&nbsp;
still it's a curious sight the shadowy man working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.600
so diligently so quietly focused singularly on his&nbsp;
craft whatever that might be only one thing could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:58.480
distract him from his efforts you he feels your&nbsp;
gaze on him and he looks up dark eyes glittering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.640
from behind a beaked ceramic mask he reminds you&nbsp;
of an illustration you once saw in a book about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.640
the black death the gear the plague doctors wore&nbsp;
while treating patients on their deathbeds hello&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.800
he greets you in a friendly heavily accented voice&nbsp;
his eyes crinkle beneath the mask and if you could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:23.120
see his mouth you know he'd be smiling how are&nbsp;
you today dear fellow are you feeling quite well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.240
he takes a step toward the window stretching out&nbsp;
one gloved hand and you suddenly realize that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:36.240
can't see where the mask ends and his skin begins&nbsp;
it's not a mask but a part of his face this is no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:44.240
ordinary man do you require help i can examine&nbsp;
you he offers palm press flat against the glass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.160
a chill runs up your spine and you realize that&nbsp;
you should definitely not take him up on his offer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.680
no matter how friendly he seems how good his&nbsp;
intentions may be you wouldn't want to let the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:01.680
plague doctor treat you he sat in his containment&nbsp;
cell fidgeting with his favorite scalpel he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:07.680
dragged it over the surface of his work table back&nbsp;
and forth listening to the sound it made they had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.840
tried to confiscate his table his tools the guards&nbsp;
had quickly learned that he had more of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:19.760
in his bag they tried to take away his bag from&nbsp;
him but well that didn't go over too well for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.840
anyone involved so he was allowed to keep it to&nbsp;
fashion himself a makeshift laboratory in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:31.120
lonely little cell there was a time where they&nbsp;
had given him test subjects fresh corpses from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:36.000
the morgue for him to dissect and research there&nbsp;
was a time when the doctors here would come to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.760
speak with him talking of cryptobiology and the&nbsp;
pestilence he had dedicated himself to fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.000
those days were long gone he had hidden away&nbsp;
pieces of the corpses tissue samples and jars of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.320
formaldehyde he could pull out when the monotony&nbsp;
became too much but the days of fresh materials of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:00.320
enlightened discourse with other men and women&nbsp;
of science were over how he missed those days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:07.040
the chance to work with others as he once had what&nbsp;
had he done wrong all he did was treat the sick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.000
sure they didn't always understand their illness&nbsp;
didn't want to receive their medicine but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.880
that wasn't a choice for the patient to make&nbsp;
that should have been up to the physician&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:22.720
perhaps they didn't trust his expertise didn't see&nbsp;
how his work served the greater good like those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.800
who watched jonas salk invent the polio vaccine&nbsp;
or louis pasteur rid milk of bacteria they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.880
confused by the advanced scientific practices&nbsp;
and feared that which they did not understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:39.920
he could forgive them for their ignorance he&nbsp;
was magnanimous that way if only they would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:46.320
let him out of this infernal room he could prove&nbsp;
his work's worth to them he could cure them all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:52.800
begin a new era of wellness and peace worldwide&nbsp;
he didn't exactly sleep but when he rested on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:04:00.720
little cot in the corner of the room he dreamed of&nbsp;
that future of a world healed by his touch a knock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.080
at the door stirred him from his reverie someone&nbsp;
someone was at the door of his containment cell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.720
he glanced at the little window and saw a guard&nbsp;
there with a tray of food he greeted the man with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:16.720
an enthusiastic wave sustenance he didn't require&nbsp;
the food for survival of course but it helped his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:22.400
mind work more efficiently it reminded him of a&nbsp;
time before these fluorescent lights and these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:28.960
same four walls of crusty bread with fresh butter&nbsp;
by the banks of the sin the little slot opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:34.400
in the door and the tray was shoved through there&nbsp;
was bread just as he hoped a small dish of butter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.560
pot of jam and a cup of tea still seeming he&nbsp;
picked up the cup at first taking a deep breath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:47.040
ah an herbal blend with fresh lavender lovely he&nbsp;
couldn't see the guard through the window anymore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.800
but he called out to him just the same thank you&nbsp;
for the libations he still had his manners after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.480
all even in confinement he wished he could have&nbsp;
gotten a better look at the man seen the power of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:04.160
his complexion a tremor in his hand he thought he&nbsp;
had spotted sweat beating on his forehead could he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.760
be ill the case required further examination to be&nbsp;
certain he sighed clutching the cup of tea tighter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:16.080
in frustration why wouldn't they just let him work&nbsp;
why must they scream at the sight of his efforts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:22.720
flee from his instruments it didn't seem&nbsp;
fair still the pursuit of science rarely was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.320
a glamorous one he had learned as much over the&nbsp;
centuries one day though history would look back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:34.080
on him kindly of this he could be certain he was&nbsp;
just settling in and beginning to spread butter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.680
across the admittedly stale bread when a horrible&nbsp;
sound shook him to attention he had heard the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:47.200
noise before though he had never seen its source&nbsp;
it was an ear splitting scream a whale of pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:54.560
agony like the sound of a wounded wild animal he&nbsp;
had heard many many screams during his life from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:59.920
patients and those who stood in the way of his&nbsp;
work but until he had been brought into custody of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:07.440
the foundation he had never heard a scream quite&nbsp;
like this one it was pure rage devastation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:14.000
suffering mixed together wet with tears and&nbsp;
loud enough to rip through human vocal folds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:21.280
whatever was crying out it was no mere man more&nbsp;
screams answered it and these were very much human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:28.080
these sounds were more familiar to him shrieks&nbsp;
of pain a fear of desperate but futile attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:34.080
to escape then the meaty thud of bodies falling&nbsp;
to the floor of torn off limbs hitting walls and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:40.800
windows a loud crash and the sound of something&nbsp;
large moving quite quickly through the halls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:45.600
scientific curiosity got the better of the doctor&nbsp;
and he found himself moving back to his little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:51.360
window face pressed to the glass so hard his beak&nbsp;
nearly cracked it he couldn't see much of anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.560
just guards running down the hall weapons drawn&nbsp;
he saw one of them fire heard the gunshot ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:02.880
out but what was he firing at then he&nbsp;
saw it a pale blur darting past the door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:07.200
whatever it was it didn't so much as flinch&nbsp;
when the bullet ricocheted off its skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.720
a long thin arm crashed against the door&nbsp;
knocking the doctor backwards into his work table&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.680
he steadied himself and climbed back to his&nbsp;
feet taking in the damage done to the door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:24.320
it was crumpled in on itself nearly ripped off the&nbsp;
hinges and whatever had plowed into it was already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:29.920
gone from the sounds of chaos in the distance it&nbsp;
had disappeared around the corner with the guards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:35.920
following it he inspected the ruins of the door&nbsp;
to his containment cell it was useless now hanging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:42.240
loose and open well that was an invitation he was&nbsp;
hardly about to decline he grabbed his trusty bag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.840
tossed his scalpel back inside and set off to see&nbsp;
what all the commotion was it was easy enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:53.200
follow the trail of blood stark and vivid red&nbsp;
against the white tile floor and the sound of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:08:00.800
gunfire human screams and that loud long painful&nbsp;
whale he had heard before he walked at a leisurely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:07.200
pace taking his time until the sound suddenly&nbsp;
stopped he rounded the corner and found a mound of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:14.400
bodies guards and scientists beaten and bloodied&nbsp;
almost beyond recognition it was quiet here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:21.840
save for one sound the sound of weeping there in&nbsp;
the corner huddled over with its face to the wall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:28.400
was a pale thin figure its shoulders heaving&nbsp;
with the force of its sobs this poor soul was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:35.120
clearly in great distress it was a peculiar sight&nbsp;
hairless and white extended arms wrapped around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:41.040
itself as it cried excuse me the doctor cried&nbsp;
out to the pitiful creature are you alright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:48.320
do you need assistance it didn't answer it just&nbsp;
continued to cry had something so despondent been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:54.720
responsible for this destruction the dozens of&nbsp;
corpses the smashed in walls the crumbled doors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.720 --> 00:09:01.120
and shattered windows it seemed impossible sure&nbsp;
it was large and looked strong but he had never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:07.040
seen a monster cry before this couldn't be&nbsp;
a dangerous creature not when it was so sad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:12.480
he would help it but first he would attend&nbsp;
to some of these bodies he sat his bag on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:18.480
the ground and pulled out several vials of liquid&nbsp;
a set of syringes and a variety of other surgical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:25.520
tools he might need now after such a long hiatus&nbsp;
he could resume his work in a meaningful way he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:30.720
couldn't be certain how long he worked reviving&nbsp;
these poor souls and reconstructing their bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:35.600
as the pale creature wept in the corner the&nbsp;
sobbing faded into the background for a while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:41.440
becoming a kind of white noise as he removed a&nbsp;
liver here placed it in a chest cavity there poked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:48.560
and prodded injected and extracted testing out new&nbsp;
methods alongside tried and true cures one by one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:54.880
the milky eyes fluttered open rigor mortis stiff&nbsp;
joints creaked into motion sallow faces looking at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.880 --> 00:10:01.120
his with the vacant gratitude he saw in so many&nbsp;
patients over the years he didn't need to thank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:07.760
him with their words the work was its own reward&nbsp;
he expected more guards to arrive to attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:14.800
contain the situation but none came even as the&nbsp;
alarm blared overhead as for the morose creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:19.760
he didn't seem to notice his presence at all&nbsp;
not even when he had brought all of the intact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:26.240
corpses back to life the patient shuffled around&nbsp;
the room aimlessly waiting for orders of some kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:32.480
the doctor tapped one on the shoulder and handed&nbsp;
the reborn man a vial of thick black medicine give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:38.320
this to the poor fellow in the corner please&nbsp;
it wasn't much but it should calm him provide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:44.480
some relief from his suffering the corpse nodded&nbsp;
mouth hanging loose and open an eyeball dangling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:50.160
unseen from the socket he shuffled over to the&nbsp;
strange creature and held out the vial to it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:56.160
it turned lifting its head and as it locked eyes&nbsp;
with the cured patient something shifted in its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:04.960
face its mouth opened wide impossibly wide and&nbsp;
a treat that same terrible sound as before tears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:11.040
streamed from its colorless eyes its arms shaking&nbsp;
with unbridled rage has its jaws locked around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:17.360
the patient's head like a boa constrictor in one&nbsp;
fluid motion it swallowed the revived man whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:23.200
while the doctor watched in shock he had been&nbsp;
wrong this was not an innocent creature caught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:30.240
in the wrong place at the wrong time this creature&nbsp;
whatever it was was deeply sick he had never seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:36.160
such an advanced aggressive case of the pestilence&nbsp;
he'd heard rumors of course but never encountered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:42.480
it firsthand as a doctor he had sworn to do no&nbsp;
harm but in a drastic situation drastic measures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:48.080
have to be taken it was well known by himself and&nbsp;
the doctors at this foundation that he could cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:54.240
any and all biological functions in an organism&nbsp;
to cease with a single touch and so he approached&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.240 --> 00:12:00.080
the creature arm outstretched ready to administer&nbsp;
that necessary touch to protect the rest of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:05.760
patients as he approached the creature turned to&nbsp;
him its eyes wide and blank an endless stream of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:11.040
tears pouring from them spilling onto the floor&nbsp;
it shrieked again mouth stretching wide enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:18.560
to engulf his entire head and ran toward him at&nbsp;
a breakneck speed i am so sorry you are not well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.600
the doctor said simply as his hand pressed&nbsp;
to the creature's chest as soon as the tough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:29.040
hide of the doctor's hand which the uninformed&nbsp;
might mistake for gloves made contact with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:36.160
unpigmented skin of the beast its eyes closed its&nbsp;
muscles went slack and it collapsed to the ground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:41.680
with a mighty thigh the doctor paced around&nbsp;
the fallen creature taking in the sight then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:48.400
something strange caught his eye the creature's&nbsp;
chest still rose and fell was it his imagination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:53.840
he checked its pulse and thought it was&nbsp;
slow and faint and though was slow and faint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.840 --> 00:13:00.720
it was very much present the creature was still&nbsp;
alive it had merely been rendered unconscious by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:09.360
his touch rather than completely deceased curious&nbsp;
very curious indeed he muttered perhaps there were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:14.880
comorbidities present other infections aside&nbsp;
from the pestilence which rendered the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:21.680
unnaturally strong resilient to the usual courses&nbsp;
of treatment what would cause these abilities this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:27.360
intense aggression it seemed to be brought on&nbsp;
whenever someone looked at the entity's face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:33.040
if only he studied psychology more the science&nbsp;
of the mind and its inner workings since he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:38.480
no experience with therapy nor was he certain this&nbsp;
creature could communicate using language at all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:43.280
there was only one way to find out more about&nbsp;
how this creature's brain worked he would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:49.360
to take it apart and see for himself it was slow&nbsp;
work getting the massive creature back to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:54.800
doctor's containment cell he required the help of&nbsp;
his cured patients who grasped it by its massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.800 --> 00:14:00.160
limbs and dragged the limp body through the halls&nbsp;
once back in a familiar environment his work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:05.440
table ready and waiting the doctor instructed his&nbsp;
assistants to place the new patient on the table&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:10.560
it was a bit small unable to accommodate the&nbsp;
creature's distended limbs but if he attempted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:16.160
to use an official foundation laboratory he&nbsp;
risked discovery and subsequent interruption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:22.160
so it would have to suffice first he set up an&nbsp;
iv stand filled with a vivid green liquid it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:27.440
was easy to find a vein the creature's skin was&nbsp;
nearly translucent now that he could be certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:32.720
the creature would not wake during surgery&nbsp;
he could make the first incision scalpel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:38.080
he held out a hand and his favorite surgical blade&nbsp;
was placed in it by one of the helpful patients&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:43.360
thank you he slid the scalpel along the hairline&nbsp;
of the creature or where the hairline would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:49.440
if it weren't completely bald once the scalp was&nbsp;
removed he set it aside for later when it could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:56.880
reattached bonsa please he held out his hand again&nbsp;
and again his assistant gave him the proper tool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:03.040
this however was when things got strange the&nbsp;
doctor had always been a deft hand at cutting he'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:08.640
once even received tutelage from the great robert&nbsp;
liston but no matter how hard he tried to saw it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:14.160
never left a scratch on the creature's skeleton&nbsp;
naturally this was somewhat frustrating he wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:19.280
to study the creature's brain tissue to get a&nbsp;
sense for what was going up there neurologically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:24.720
and he couldn't do that if it was impossible to&nbsp;
saw off the creature's cranial cap he blunted two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:29.920
of his favorite saws while trying thankfully there&nbsp;
was still a solution to access the beast's gray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:35.760
matter a little trick he learned while studying&nbsp;
the funerary practices of the ancient egyptians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.520
he produced a long curved hook from his bag&nbsp;
and inserted it up the creature's nasal passage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:46.880
with some fine maneuvering he eventually managed&nbsp;
to remove the brain it was such a terrible shame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:52.320
that he needed to do it piece by piece via the&nbsp;
nasal passage but one makes do all that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:57.840
left was to sew the skin of the creature's head&nbsp;
back into place it was mid-stitch when a voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:03.680
interrupted his careful work nearly making him&nbsp;
drop the needle hey what are you doing he looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:10.240
up to find a guard aiming a gun at his face excuse&nbsp;
me i am in surgery at the moment please do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:16.240
interrupt he admonished the guard but the man did&nbsp;
not listen or lower his weapon in fact he shouted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:21.600
something into the radio code words the doctor&nbsp;
didn't recognize then he fired a bullet into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:29.040
skull of the patient standing at his side how dare&nbsp;
you the doctor cried readying himself to confront&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:34.160
the guard but it was too late dozens of other&nbsp;
guards were swarming the room and neutralizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:39.600
his assistance some in hazmat suits grabbed his&nbsp;
arms and pulled him away from the creature on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:46.320
operating table no matter how hard he fought or&nbsp;
how loudly he protested then something incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:52.960
happened something wonderful the creature opened&nbsp;
its eyes and sat up it looked directly at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:59.760
guard closest to it and the two saw one another's&nbsp;
faces the guard tensed preparing for the worst but&nbsp;&nbsp;

